{
  "id": "Compound::DB00281 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Lidocaine exhibits a complex interaction with Cyp3a4 through multiple mechanistic pathways, primarily involving cytochrome P450 enzymes. The evidence suggests that Lidocaine binds to Cyp2c18 and Cyp2c8, which are both involved in the metabolism of steroid hydroxylase activity and oxidoreductase activity, respectively. These enzymes are known to be part of the Cyp3a4 family, indicating a potential role in the metabolic activation of substrates. The final scores from the paths highlight a consistent interaction between Lidocaine and Cyp3a4, suggesting a biologically relevant relationship. The overlapping pathways imply that Lidocaine may modulate the activity of Cyp3a4 through the activation of different Cyp subfamily members, which in turn affects the metabolism of various substrates. This integrated evidence supports the notion that Lidocaine's interaction with Cyp3a4 is mediated through the activation of multiple Cyp enzymes, contributing to its potential effects on steroid metabolism.",
